SVELTE REACTIVITY TRAP, the important one:

  {@const offset = offsetOf(i)}   // offsetOf() closes over `active`

  Svelte tracks only the identifiers VISIBLE IN THE EXPRESSION. It saw
  `offsetOf` and `i`, never `active`, so the const was computed once and never
  recomputed. The counter and the active-card border still updated because
  those read `active` directly in the template — so the wheel highlighted a
  new card while every card transform stayed frozen.

  Fix: a reactive statement that references `active` and `items` directly.
  Rule: if a template value depends on state only through a function call, the
  compiler cannot see it. Compute it in a `$:` block instead.

I ALSO VERIFIED THIS WRONG, which is why it shipped. My test asserted the
counter text advanced — a code path that was never broken. The test now
snapshots the slots' --ow-y custom properties before/after and asserts they
differ. Lesson: assert on the thing the user sees move, not on a proxy that
